  "version": 1,
  "doc": "D-341 rosy-pair/1 shared vectors (19). Machine source for the confirmation code, the site fingerprint, the request/reveal/result JSON shapes and the pairable-record rule; read by core_common.protocol.pairing (Fleet, Vision) and the Rosy Cam Kotlin tests. Code: SHA-256 over six UTF-8 fields, each prefixed by its byte length as 4-byte big-endian unsigned (\"rosy-pair/1\", role, request_id, leaf_cert_sha256, client_nonce, server_nonce); decimal6 = first 8 digest bytes as big-endian unsigned integer mod 1000000, zero-padded to 6 digits. leaf_cert_sha256 is the lowercase hex SHA-256 of the leaf certificate DER as text. Nonces, poll secret and token are 32 random bytes as base64url without padding (43 chars). client_commit and poll_secret_sha256 are lowercase hex SHA-256 of the ASCII nonce/secret text. Fingerprint: CA DER SHA-256, first 16 hex upper case, groups of 4 joined by '-'. Request and reveal bodies reject unknown fields (extra=forbid); a request body over 4096 bytes is too_large before it is parsed (over_4_kib: measure the compact UTF-8 JSON). A result accepts and ignores unknown fields; its site_ca_pem must be the site CA (every block basicConstraints cA=TRUE, site-link rule), never a leaf. Pairable: a discovery record that core_common discovery_txt accepts as _rosy-overhead._tcp and whose TXT has pair=rosy-pair/1; a rejected record keeps the discovery reason. Each invalid case has one fault. Long values sit on lines naming sha256/digest so the repository secret scan reads them as integrity data; nothing here is a live credential.",
